  "description": "A Unit Of Measure is a definite magnitude of a Physical Quantity Type, defined and adopted by convention or by law, that is used as a standard for measurement of the same Physical Quantity Type.\n\nAny other value of the Physical Quantity Type can be expressed as a simple multiple of the Unit Of Measure. For example, length is a Physical Quantity Type. The meter is a Unit Of Measure of length that represents a definite predetermined length. When it says 10 meters (or 10m), it actually means 10 times the definite predetermined length called \u201cmeter\u201d. (Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Units_of_measurement)",
